set_markup.md:
Sets the labels text and attributes from markup.

The string must be marked up with Pango markup
(see `parse_markup`).

If `str` is external data, you may need to escape it
with `markup_escape_text` or `markup_printf_escaped`:

```c
GtkWidget *self = gtk_label_new (NULL);
const char *str = "...";
const char *format = "<span style=\"italic\">\%s</span>";
char *markup;

markup = g_markup_printf_escaped (format, str);
gtk_label_set_markup (GTK_LABEL (self), markup);
g_free (markup);
```

This function sets the [`Label:use-markup`](xref:gtk:Gtk.Label#property:use-markup) property
to true.

Also see [`Label.set_text()`](xref:gtk:Gtk.Label#method:set_text).
